From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000003 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MinsOS <minsos@local>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Register the face@2.0 HAL as a weak biometric, like stock y2q (One UI 9)

AuthService$Injector.getConfiguration() registers the HIDL face sensor as
"1:8:4095" (BIOMETRIC_CONVENIENCE) when SemBiometricFeature.FEATURE_JDM_HAL is
set and "1:8:255" (BIOMETRIC_WEAK) otherwise, the same rule as stock SM-G986N
A13 Utils. Stock y2q is in_house, so its face was weak; y2q sets jdm only to
load the V2_0 face HAL class. Read the flag as false for the face strength
only. The fingerprint line above it is left on jdm.
---
diff --git a/smali/com/android/server/biometrics/AuthService$Injector.smali b/smali/com/android/server/biometrics/AuthService$Injector.smali
index 73225df..c666fdc 100644
--- a/smali/com/android/server/biometrics/AuthService$Injector.smali
+++ b/smali/com/android/server/biometrics/AuthService$Injector.smali
@@ -89,7 +89,7 @@
     invoke-virtual {p0, p1}, Ljava/util/ArrayList;->add(Ljava/lang/Object;)Z
 
     :cond_2
-    sget-boolean p1, Lcom/android/server/biometrics/SemBiometricFeature;->FEATURE_JDM_HAL:Z
+    const/4 p1, 0x0
 
     if-eqz p1, :cond_3
 
-- 
2.45.0
